 ## Operating characteristics
-- **Time Complexity:** Not given in the sources. [G] The algorithm performs $O(N + M)$ set operations and allocations, where $N$ is the number of chunks in the render distance and $M$ is the number of currently loaded chunks.
-- **Memory Complexity:** Not given in the sources. [G] Auxiliary space is $O(N + M)$ for the position sets, plus proportional to the number of loaded chunks.
-- **Strengths:** Simple, deterministic, and easy to implement. It guarantees that no chunk within the render distance is missing and no chunk outside is present [S1, unofficial].
-- **Limitations:** It does not handle asynchronous I/O scheduling or priority. It assumes that chunk generation and draw call management are implemented elsewhere [S1, unofficial].
